  "answer": "Yes—as Manual practice, examiners should check the trade mark (rather than the goods themselves) against both the INN list and the INN stems when examining Class 5 applications covering pharmaceuticals or veterinary substances. Use the Search for International Nonproprietary Names for Pharmaceutical Substances and the INN stems list in Annex 1 to Part 29 [TMM/Part29/5/5/3].\n\nThe Manual also identifies claims such as analgesics, pain relieving preparations, and potentially pharmaceutical or veterinary goods such as dietary or nutritional supplements as potentially triggering section 43 considerations concerning INNs and INN stems [TMM/Part29/5/5/3]. This checking direction is Manual practice, not a legislative requirement stated in the supplied Act passages."
